eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-02-09T12:59:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T04:24:07Z","closed_at":"2026-02-12T04:24:07Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.stable \n- Not reproducible in: 4.5.1.stable \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable (89cea1439) - Fedora Linux 43 (i3) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn Linux (X11), the inline rename popup in the editor (e.g. when renaming a node in the Scene dock) appears near the center of the editor window instead of being positioned relative to the UI element that triggered it.\n\nIn earlier versions, the rename popup appeared anchored close to the Scene dock node being renamed. In newer builds, it appears detached from the Scene dock, which makes renaming feel visually disconnected and less intuitive.\n\ngodot 4.5.1.stable:\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"845\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae845d59-b841-432a-a1f1-89e42061066f\" />\n\ngodot 4.6.stable:\n<img width=\"1595\" height=\"865\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d0cf32e-f51c-4589-aed1-166b26dde083\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen Godot Editor on Linux distro with i3 WM.\n\nCreate a new empty project.\n\nAdd a Node2D to the scene.\n\nClick the node name in the Scene dock and press Rename or press F2.\n\nObserve the position of the rename popup.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":